{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/7SwiftUI4ViewP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MISOBulletList","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/ContentDisplay"],"kind":"mentions"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Types","level":2,"anchor":"Types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three types are proposed:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unordered (by default)"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Collects related items that don’t need to be in a specific order or sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Collects related items with numeric order or sequence."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bare"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": An unordered list without any bullets or alphanumeric sequence.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Types can be mixed in list, but must be identical for the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MISOBulletList.NestedLevel"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Levels","level":2,"anchor":"Levels"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Lists can include nested items to indicate hierarchy or subcategories, with indentation distinguishing each level."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Arrange ordered list items logically, such as ranking by importance, highest to lowest values, or in alphabetical \/ numeric order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Three levels are maximum."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Text Style","level":2,"anchor":"Text-Style"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"List can be used with different font sizes:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Body Large","type":"text"}]},{"text":": If the text accompanying the list component is the Body Large text. This variant is designed for more visual, engaging experiences.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Body Medium"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": If the text accompanying the list component is the Body Medium text. This variant is best suited for functional, task-oriented experiences.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Cases-forbidden-by-design","text":"Cases forbidden by design","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"it is not allowed to have a depth of items greater than 3","type":"text"}]}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Internationalisation-considerations","text":"Internationalisation considerations","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For latin-based speaking countries, like France, Spain, United Kingdom or Belgium, the european “arabic” numbers are used for the first level of depth"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the ordered bullet list. For the second and third levels, the european alphabets are used with upper and lower case values."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"However for countries speaking arabic, these rules can’t be applied. Indeed, there is no notion of upper and lower case characters in arabic alphabet.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In addition, the numbers in use (i.e. the european “arabic” numbers like “1, 2, 3”) are accepted in arabic countries, even if the “true arabic” numbers (like “ ٢ ٣ ١”) are used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in middle-east arabic countries and for official documents.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Thus the MISO ordered bullet list will use “european” numbers for first level, and arabic alphabets for second and third levels.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Code-samples","text":"Code samples","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["       \/\/ 1. Unordered list with bullets","       MISOBulletList {","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 2\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 3\")","       }","","       \/\/ 1.1. Item of Unordered list with bullet as tick, a text style","       \/\/ body medium and text bold","       MISOBulletList(type: .unordered(asset: .tick),","                      textStyle: .bodyMedium,","                      isBold: true)  {","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 2\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 3\")","       }","","       \/\/ 2. Bare list with 3 items","       MISOBulletList(type: .bare) {","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 2\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 3\")","       }","","       \/\/ 3. Ordered list with 3 items","       MISOBulletList(type: .ordered) {","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 2\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 3\")","       }","","       \/\/ 3.1. Ordered list with 3 items in first level,","       \/\/ and one item as sub item (second level),","       \/\/ and 2 items as sub item in (third level)","       MISOBulletList(type: .ordered) {","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1\") {","               MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1.1\") {","                   MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1.1.1\")","                   MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1.1.2\")","               }","           }","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 2\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 3\")","       }","","       \/\/ Same Bullet list but items in third level with free icon as bullet","       let icon = Image(decorative: \"ic_heart\")","       MISOBulletList(type: .ordered) {","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1\") {","               MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1.1\", subListType: .unordered(asset: .icon(icon))) {","                   MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1.1.1\")","                   MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 1.1.2\")","               }","           }","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 2\")","           MISOBulletList.Item(\"Label 3\")","       }"]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Rich-text-recommendations","text":"Rich text recommendations","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Rich text can be applied for bullet list whatever the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isBold"},{"text":" flag is.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Strong text can be used sparingly within alert messages to highlight key information.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Underlined text must not be used for emphasis, as it is commonly associated with links.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Underlined links must be bold.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If a hyperlink is needed within the content, the underlined style should be used.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Italic should be used with care, some brands do not allow it.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"No other text styles should be used.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Accessibility-considerations","text":"Accessibility considerations"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Always check the results of rich text mode with high contrast, light and dark modes, and Voice Over vocalization."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"1.1.0 (Figma component design version)","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Version"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS 1.2.0","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Since"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MISOBulletList","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"externalID":"s:14MISOComponents14MISOBulletListV","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"MISOBulletList","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MISOBulletList","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":[{"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"16.0","deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS","beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"introducedAt":"11.0","deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","beta":false}]},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOBulletList"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/misocomponents\/misobulletlist"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentation\/MISOComponents\/MISOBulletList\/Item"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MISOComponents\/documentat